 "segments": [
  {
   "id": "sotah.21b.4",
   "daf": "21b",
   "sentenceId": 3,
   "he": "רַבִּי יְהוֹשֻׁעַ אוֹמֵר: רוֹצָה אִשָּׁה וְכוּ׳. מַאי קָאָמַר? הָכִי קָאָמַר: רוֹצָה אִשָּׁה בְּקַב וְתִיפְלוּת עִמּוֹ, מִתִּשְׁעַת קַבִּין וּפְרִישׁוּת.",
   "en": "§ The mishna states that «Rabbi Yehoshua says: A woman desires» to receive the amount of a kav of food and a sexual relationship rather than to receive nine kav of food and abstinence. The Gemara asks: «What is he saying? This is what» Rabbi Yehoshua «is saying: A woman desires to» receive the amount of «a kav» of food «and with it a sexual relationship,» i.e., her husband’s availability to fulfill her sexual desires, rather «than nine kav» of food «and» with it «abstinence,» and since her desires are of a sexual nature, it is undesirable for her to study Torah."
  }
